From: sunuazizrahayu <sunuazizrahayu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] cmds: Drop vibrator-lge tool requiring removed HIDL vibrator

The vibrator-lge helper links against vendor.lge.hardware.vibrator@1.0,
whose android.hardware.vibrator@1.0 dependency no longer exists in this
tree (migrated to AIDL). The tool is not part of any product package,
so drop its definition instead of carrying the stale HAL.
---
 cmds/Android.bp | 12 ------------
 1 file changed, 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmds/Android.bp b/cmds/Android.bp
--- a/cmds/Android.bp
+++ b/cmds/Android.bp
@@ -36,19 +36,7 @@
 	],
 	host_supported: true,
 }
 
-cc_binary {
-	name: "vibrator-lge",
-	srcs: [
-		"vibrator-lge.cpp",
-	],
-	shared_libs: [
-		"vendor.lge.hardware.vibrator@1.0",
-		"libutils",
-		"libhidlbase",
-	],
-}
-
 cc_binary {
 	name: "mtk-sms-fwk-ready",
 	srcs: [
-- 
